1
00:00:07,665 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:38,985
ADAPTED FROM THE EARLY SPRING ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:53,185 --> 00:01:54,345
Luke!

4
00:02:00,065 --> 00:02:02,265
Look. Just look at what you've done.

5
00:02:03,065 --> 00:02:03,905
Have you lost your mind?

6
00:02:06,105 --> 00:02:06,945
Don't move.

7
00:02:09,665 --> 00:02:10,785
I'm gonna smack you.

8
00:02:10,864 --> 00:02:12,065
Take that.

9
00:02:13,105 --> 00:02:14,305
Let's see if you dare do it again.

10
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:17,785
Next time you trash the place,

11
00:02:17,865 --> 00:02:20,185
I'll throw you out and let you be a stray.

12
00:02:24,745 --> 00:02:25,745
Playing pitiful now?

13
00:02:28,225 --> 00:02:29,465
Just like your mom.

14
00:02:30,025 --> 00:02:30,945
Come here!

15
00:02:41,625 --> 00:02:42,665
Don't give me that.

16
00:02:55,985 --> 00:02:56,905
All right.

17
00:03:01,225 --> 00:03:02,105
Have a treat.

18
00:03:10,545 --> 00:03:11,625
Paw.

19
00:03:14,025 --> 00:03:14,865
And this one.

20
00:03:15,385 --> 00:03:18,625
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED
DURING THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

21
00:03:19,945 --> 00:03:20,825
What happened to your paw?

22
00:03:23,425 --> 00:03:24,585
Does it hurt?

23
00:03:25,185 --> 00:03:26,305
Does it hurt, Luke?

24
00:03:30,945 --> 00:03:31,825
It's okay.

25
00:03:35,225 --> 00:03:36,145
Hello?

26
00:03:37,065 --> 00:03:38,785
Has your dog's paw ever lost fur?

27
00:03:39,345 --> 00:03:40,625
Will it kill him?

28
00:03:40,705 --> 00:03:41,785
Oh no. It's terminal.

29
00:03:44,985 --> 00:03:46,185
What should I do?

30
00:03:46,265 --> 00:03:47,185
Which hospital should I take him to?

31
00:03:48,825 --> 00:03:50,865
I'm messing with you. Relax.

32
00:03:50,945 --> 00:03:52,625
Ms. Shang's dog is a lucky one.

33
00:03:52,705 --> 00:03:53,945
How could anything happen to him?

34
00:03:54,025 --> 00:03:55,345
It's probably just inflamed.

35
00:03:55,425 --> 00:03:56,985
Put some iodine on it
and keep an eye on it.

36
00:03:57,065 --> 00:03:58,145
Don't worry.

37
00:04:03,345 --> 00:04:05,745
You'll be fine. Come on.
Let's put some medicine on your paw.

38
00:04:07,345 --> 00:04:08,385
Let's go.

39
00:04:09,905 --> 00:04:10,745
Over here.

40
00:04:12,265 --> 00:04:15,665
THINKING OF YOU THIS SECOND
SEEING YOU THE NEXT

41
00:04:19,985 --> 00:04:21,865
Sit. Come here.

42
00:04:26,865 --> 00:04:27,945
Sit.

43
00:04:29,505 --> 00:04:30,345
Sit.

44
00:04:32,065 --> 00:04:32,985
Come on, let's put some medicine on it.

45
00:04:33,625 --> 00:04:34,865
You can eat after we're done.

46
00:04:35,545 --> 00:04:36,385
Give me your paw.

47
00:04:38,025 --> 00:04:39,065
Come on.

48
00:04:40,185 --> 00:04:41,465
Hold still.

49
00:04:44,305 --> 00:04:45,705
Good. Almost done.

50
00:04:46,905 --> 00:04:48,025
Let me see.

51
00:04:52,145 --> 00:04:53,745
All done. Here.

52
00:04:56,025 --> 00:04:57,185
Eat.

53
00:04:59,625 --> 00:05:00,625
Sit.

54
00:05:00,705 --> 00:05:01,625
Sit.

55
00:05:03,225 --> 00:05:04,185
Eat.

56
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:06,865
ZANG YAO

57
00:05:09,745 --> 00:05:11,145
I'm leaving.

58
00:05:11,225 --> 00:05:12,505
Want to meet?

59
00:05:16,105 --> 00:05:17,065
Sure.

60
00:05:29,865 --> 00:05:31,505
The meat here really is different.

61
00:05:31,585 --> 00:05:32,425
It smells amazing.

62
00:05:44,305 --> 00:05:45,625
Need a hand?

63
00:05:45,705 --> 00:05:46,585
No.

64
00:05:49,305 --> 00:05:53,785
Your window is held together with tape?

65
00:05:55,665 --> 00:05:56,865
It seals the gaps.

66
00:05:57,545 --> 00:05:59,265
What made you suddenly decide
to come see me?

67
00:06:01,425 --> 00:06:03,505
Wasn't I in Inner Mongolia
looking for investors?

68
00:06:04,185 --> 00:06:05,545
I figured I wasn't that far from you.

69
00:06:05,625 --> 00:06:08,025
Just a train ride away.

70
00:06:08,585 --> 00:06:09,465
So I came to see you.

71
00:06:11,065 --> 00:06:15,185
Twelve hours by train
isn't exactly nearby.

72
00:06:18,065 --> 00:06:19,145
True enough.

73
00:06:20,385 --> 00:06:21,265
It was so last minute.

74
00:06:22,025 --> 00:06:23,385
The sleeper tickets were sold out.

75
00:06:23,465 --> 00:06:24,825
I sat the whole way here.

76
00:06:24,905 --> 00:06:26,225
My back is killing me.

77
00:06:29,105 --> 00:06:31,225
Is there a hotel nearby?

78
00:06:32,145 --> 00:06:34,185
I'll settle in for the night first.

79
00:06:34,745 --> 00:06:37,225
The nearest guesthouse
is three hours away.

80
00:06:37,825 --> 00:06:38,985
Three hours?

81
00:06:41,865 --> 00:06:42,985
Then what do we do?

82
00:06:48,465 --> 00:06:49,545
-You sleep here.
-I'll sleep over there.

83
00:06:49,625 --> 00:06:51,265
-You take the bed.
-You…

84
00:06:51,345 --> 00:06:52,785
I'll take the couch.

85
00:06:52,865 --> 00:06:54,705
-I'll take the couch.
-I'll…

86
00:06:56,985 --> 00:06:58,025
Let's eat first.

87
00:06:58,545 --> 00:06:59,665
Okay.

88
00:07:03,785 --> 00:07:05,105
Try this.

89
00:07:18,305 --> 00:07:19,305
Sit.

90
00:07:25,265 --> 00:07:27,385
Weren't you planning to stay
in Beijing for another two years?

91
00:07:31,465 --> 00:07:32,345
Not anymore.

92
00:07:38,145 --> 00:07:38,985
Whose dog is this?

93
00:07:40,305 --> 00:07:41,225
Mine.

94
00:07:43,425 --> 00:07:44,625
I've known you for years.

95
00:07:44,705 --> 00:07:46,105
You'd never get a dog.

96
00:07:46,185 --> 00:07:47,745
If you were going to get one,
it'd be a Tibetan Mastiff.

97
00:07:50,865 --> 00:07:51,945
It's Shang Zhitao's dog, isn't it?

98
00:07:53,065 --> 00:07:54,865
Yeah. It's her dog.

99
00:07:58,105 --> 00:07:59,105
When are you leaving?

100
00:08:00,345 --> 00:08:01,185
The day after tomorrow.

101
00:08:02,185 --> 00:08:03,025
So soon?

102
00:08:05,145 --> 00:08:06,345
Beijing isn't interesting anymore.

103
00:08:07,065 --> 00:08:08,345
I'm going back to the UK.

104
00:08:09,345 --> 00:08:10,585
At this point,

105
00:08:11,265 --> 00:08:14,665
Beijing doesn't really have anything
to do with me anymore.

106
00:08:17,225 --> 00:08:18,065
Have you made up your mind?

107
00:08:21,545 --> 00:08:24,065
Whether I have or not,
would it change anything?

108
00:08:26,345 --> 00:08:28,425
I came back for you.

109
00:08:29,305 --> 00:08:31,465
But if you're no longer
the person you used to be,

110
00:08:31,545 --> 00:08:33,385
how could I force you?

111
00:08:34,545 --> 00:08:35,985
Or are you saying that to make me stay,

112
00:08:36,664 --> 00:08:38,144
you'd give me what I've always wanted?

113
00:08:44,865 --> 00:08:46,265
He's pretty loyal.

114
00:08:46,345 --> 00:08:47,625
Keeping an eye on you for his owner.

115
00:08:50,385 --> 00:08:52,945
Then I wish you a safe journey

116
00:08:53,505 --> 00:08:55,105
and that everything
goes your way from now on.

117
00:08:58,785 --> 00:08:59,825
Luan Nian.

118
00:09:01,545 --> 00:09:04,145
Won't you give me one last hug?

119
00:09:21,745 --> 00:09:22,825
All right.

120
00:09:23,345 --> 00:09:24,225
Let's go.

121
00:09:28,385 --> 00:09:29,425
Go.

122
00:09:31,105 --> 00:09:32,145
Go.

123
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:48,705
Go.

124
00:09:54,945 --> 00:09:55,865
Luan Nian.

125
00:09:56,465 --> 00:09:57,385
Goodbye.

126
00:09:59,225 --> 00:10:00,865
Keeping an eye on me for your owner, huh?

127
00:10:02,305 --> 00:10:03,625
What are we now?

128
00:10:03,705 --> 00:10:04,625
Why would you do that?

129
00:10:08,505 --> 00:10:09,385
Let's go home.

130
00:10:09,905 --> 00:10:10,985
Come on.

131
00:10:40,425 --> 00:10:41,465
Yuanzhu.

132
00:10:42,465 --> 00:10:43,545
Are you sleepy?

133
00:10:46,105 --> 00:10:47,825
I'm a little scared.

134
00:10:49,305 --> 00:10:50,625
I can't fall asleep.

135
00:10:53,625 --> 00:10:55,625
I thought nothing ever scared you.

136
00:10:57,425 --> 00:10:58,505
Listen.

137
00:10:59,625 --> 00:11:01,425
Listen to the wind
rustling the window paper.

138
00:11:02,105 --> 00:11:03,505
Then start counting.

139
00:11:04,025 --> 00:11:07,025
One, two, three.

140
00:11:07,705 --> 00:11:08,825
You'll be asleep before you know it.

141
00:11:09,545 --> 00:11:10,585
Give it a try.

142
00:11:27,545 --> 00:11:29,105
I still can't sleep.

143
00:11:29,185 --> 00:11:31,905
How about you keep me company for a while?

144
00:11:34,025 --> 00:11:34,865
Go ahead.

145
00:11:36,785 --> 00:11:38,905
When you're away on business by yourself,

146
00:11:39,945 --> 00:11:41,225
do you miss home?

147
00:11:46,905 --> 00:11:47,865
Of course I do.

148
00:11:50,145 --> 00:11:53,185
Your hometown is up
in the mountains, right?

149
00:11:54,345 --> 00:11:57,465
After this business trip,
I'll go back with you and take a look.

150
00:11:57,545 --> 00:11:59,585
I meant my home in Beijing.

151
00:12:02,705 --> 00:12:05,785
Aren't you, Lei, and Tao my family?

152
00:12:10,785 --> 00:12:13,145
Of course we are.

153
00:12:24,185 --> 00:12:25,225
Yuanzhu.

154
00:12:28,425 --> 00:12:29,385
Mr. Genius.

155
00:12:30,985 --> 00:12:36,545
Do you think I'm a good person?

156
00:12:39,505 --> 00:12:40,945
You are.

157
00:12:41,025 --> 00:12:44,145
You're my best friend and family.

158
00:12:55,105 --> 00:12:56,505
Look.

159
00:12:56,585 --> 00:13:02,545
We've been living under the same roof
for over three years.

160
00:13:03,825 --> 00:13:05,905
I really like your cooking.

161
00:13:08,825 --> 00:13:11,745
And I don't think you dislike me either.

162
00:13:13,985 --> 00:13:16,185
Honestly…

163
00:13:17,145 --> 00:13:19,625
When friends and family come to see me,
it makes me really happy.

164
00:13:20,145 --> 00:13:21,985
Especially you. You're my best friend.

165
00:13:24,145 --> 00:13:24,985
How about this?

166
00:13:25,065 --> 00:13:27,665
Tomorrow afternoon I'll take you
for lamb with Mongolian chives.

167
00:13:27,745 --> 00:13:29,105
It's our most authentic local specialty.

168
00:13:29,185 --> 00:13:30,425
Then I'll take you to the station.

169
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:33,305
Or I can book you a hotel
for tomorrow night.

170
00:13:33,385 --> 00:13:34,745
You can stay
a couple more days if you want.

171
00:13:35,585 --> 00:13:37,785
It's just that I have work
these next two days,

172
00:13:37,865 --> 00:13:39,145
so I probably won't be able
to keep you company.

173
00:13:39,865 --> 00:13:40,945
Don't be mad at me.

174
00:13:47,625 --> 00:13:49,425
Don't say things like that.

175
00:13:50,145 --> 00:13:51,705
It doesn't sound sincere.

176
00:13:53,865 --> 00:13:56,905
If anyone should apologize,
it should be me.

177
00:13:56,985 --> 00:13:59,985
Don't be upset that I suddenly showed up
and caused you trouble.

178
00:14:05,225 --> 00:14:07,345
You don't need to worry about me tomorrow.

179
00:14:07,425 --> 00:14:08,385
I'll just look around on my own.

180
00:14:11,705 --> 00:14:12,985
And I'll…

181
00:14:13,065 --> 00:14:15,465
I'll… I'll buy my own ticket back.

182
00:14:15,545 --> 00:14:16,625
You don't have to worry about me.

183
00:14:17,185 --> 00:14:18,025
I'll get the ticket.

184
00:14:19,585 --> 00:14:21,025
It's late. Get some sleep.

185
00:14:21,545 --> 00:14:23,025
You've had a long day.

186
00:14:23,785 --> 00:14:25,105
I'm a little tired too.

187
00:14:29,625 --> 00:14:30,825
Good night.

188
00:14:47,145 --> 00:14:48,825
The wind really is strong.

189
00:14:51,745 --> 00:14:53,185
Let's count.

190
00:14:55,305 --> 00:14:56,585
Didn't you say

191
00:14:58,025 --> 00:14:59,745
counting helps you fall asleep?

192
00:15:01,505 --> 00:15:02,505
One.

193
00:15:03,985 --> 00:15:05,105
Two.

194
00:15:06,065 --> 00:15:06,945
Three.

195
00:15:10,745 --> 00:15:11,785
Four.

196
00:15:13,545 --> 00:15:14,505
Five.

197
00:15:15,545 --> 00:15:16,385
Six.

198
00:15:18,385 --> 00:15:19,425
Seven.

199
00:15:29,945 --> 00:15:31,265
How's Luke?

200
00:15:31,345 --> 00:15:32,705
Is his paw still inflamed?

201
00:15:35,025 --> 00:15:35,905
Not good.

202
00:15:37,065 --> 00:15:38,745
How could it not be?

203
00:15:39,745 --> 00:15:41,145
Let me see him.

204
00:15:42,185 --> 00:15:43,265
Here.

205
00:15:47,185 --> 00:15:49,265
See? He's perfectly fine. You're lying.

206
00:15:49,865 --> 00:15:50,705
Luke.

207
00:15:52,425 --> 00:15:53,825
That silly dog does nothing but bark.

208
00:15:53,905 --> 00:15:54,745
He's so noisy.

209
00:15:56,265 --> 00:15:59,345
Well, how are you?

210
00:16:00,985 --> 00:16:02,865
Still alive. Getting by.

211
00:16:03,545 --> 00:16:04,585
How about you?

212
00:16:05,105 --> 00:16:06,345
You are calling this late.

213
00:16:06,425 --> 00:16:07,625
Are you working overtime?

214
00:16:10,945 --> 00:16:12,385
How's the work environment in Hangzhou?

215
00:16:13,025 --> 00:16:14,105
Getting used to the new team?

216
00:16:16,025 --> 00:16:17,345
Do you want the truth or a lie?

217
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:20,105
The truth.

218
00:16:24,145 --> 00:16:27,945
I think Dony
is a very clear-headed leader.

219
00:16:28,025 --> 00:16:30,545
The instructions he gives everyone
are always very clear.

220
00:16:32,865 --> 00:16:35,225
You'll be sold down the river
and still thank them for it.

221
00:16:36,785 --> 00:16:39,745
Look at you. You asked for the truth.

222
00:16:39,825 --> 00:16:42,385
I'm just trying to know my opponent
before the battle.

223
00:16:42,985 --> 00:16:44,105
What battle?

224
00:16:45,025 --> 00:16:46,025
He's your boss.

225
00:16:48,065 --> 00:16:49,825
You seem pretty hostile toward him.

226
00:16:50,985 --> 00:16:52,185
Do you two have history?

227
00:16:53,545 --> 00:16:54,585
No.

228
00:16:54,665 --> 00:16:55,585
From now on, when you call,

229
00:16:55,665 --> 00:16:57,505
don't sound like
you're reporting to your boss.

230
00:16:59,425 --> 00:17:01,185
Just tell me when you're coming back.

231
00:17:01,785 --> 00:17:02,745
I'll be waiting for you.

232
00:17:04,065 --> 00:17:05,305
I'll come back as soon as I'm done.

233
00:17:41,265 --> 00:17:44,745
I just meant that in the workplace,
no one's doing anyone a favor.

234
00:17:44,825 --> 00:17:46,425
There's no need to act
like you're above everyone else.

235
00:17:49,865 --> 00:17:50,745
Don't catch a cold.

236
00:17:51,825 --> 00:17:52,825
You should head back.

237
00:17:54,665 --> 00:17:56,345
These are your New Year's gifts.

238
00:17:56,425 --> 00:17:57,545
How about I treat you?

239
00:17:57,625 --> 00:17:59,025
Let's go see a movie tonight.

240
00:17:59,625 --> 00:18:00,665
You said it.

241
00:18:01,305 --> 00:18:03,665
It wasn't easy for the four of us
to become friends.

242
00:18:04,345 --> 00:18:06,065
We'll always look out for you.

243
00:18:09,065 --> 00:18:10,945
Every gathering must come to an end.

244
00:18:11,465 --> 00:18:13,025
People come and go.

245
00:18:14,825 --> 00:18:16,385
That's just part of life.

246
00:18:54,225 --> 00:18:57,305
What do you think of Dony's abilities?

247
00:18:57,385 --> 00:18:58,105
DONY'S CV

248
00:18:59,665 --> 00:19:00,585
I've heard he's pretty capable.

249
00:19:00,665 --> 00:19:05,185
He's very clear-headed
and has a clear strategy for the division.

250
00:19:06,505 --> 00:19:08,505
Are you complimenting him?

251
00:19:09,185 --> 00:19:11,465
At the meeting last time,

252
00:19:11,545 --> 00:19:13,585
I thought you were pretty hard on him.

253
00:19:14,585 --> 00:19:15,705
Did you know each other before?

254
00:19:17,425 --> 00:19:19,145
Yes, but I'd rather never meet him again.

255
00:19:21,225 --> 00:19:23,985
You don't think he came
to Lime because of you, do you?

256
00:19:25,785 --> 00:19:26,945
Let's hope not.

257
00:19:27,465 --> 00:19:29,465
I've worked in HR
at Lime for so many years.

258
00:19:29,545 --> 00:19:30,825
He's the first person
who didn't go through

259
00:19:30,905 --> 00:19:32,825
our HR department
before being assigned here.

260
00:19:33,745 --> 00:19:36,105
And as soon as he arrived,
he took over your New Media team.

261
00:19:36,625 --> 00:19:39,865
I don't think it's that simple.

262
00:19:42,985 --> 00:19:44,345
Did you do a background check on him?

263
00:19:45,305 --> 00:19:46,945
He was hired directly by the board.

264
00:19:47,025 --> 00:19:48,465
How was our department
supposed to do a background check?

265
00:19:49,465 --> 00:19:50,945
Then I suggest you do it.

266
00:19:51,745 --> 00:19:52,905
You might find a surprise.

267
00:19:55,305 --> 00:19:56,305
Don't worry.

268
00:19:57,065 --> 00:19:58,665
I'm already looking into it.

269
00:20:12,625 --> 00:20:13,465
Come eat.

270
00:20:19,865 --> 00:20:21,025
Here.

271
00:20:23,745 --> 00:20:25,745
The meat pie's hot. Eat slowly.

272
00:20:26,425 --> 00:20:27,465
Don't burn your mouth.

273
00:20:33,345 --> 00:20:35,145
Slow down. I'm not
going to take it from you.

274
00:20:35,745 --> 00:20:36,785
Have some vegetables.

275
00:20:39,225 --> 00:20:40,065
Silly dog.

276
00:20:50,025 --> 00:20:51,025
Hello?

277
00:20:52,185 --> 00:20:53,665
Your silly dog is eating the meat pie.

278
00:20:54,265 --> 00:20:55,105
Have you eaten?

279
00:20:55,625 --> 00:20:56,825
What are you having for dinner?

280
00:20:58,225 --> 00:20:59,465
I'm going to stir-fry a couple of dishes.

281
00:21:00,105 --> 00:21:02,025
And make some osmanthus milk.

282
00:21:02,825 --> 00:21:03,865
Why?

283
00:21:04,545 --> 00:21:05,625
You want some?

284
00:21:08,985 --> 00:21:10,505
Then come back soon if you do.

285
00:21:10,585 --> 00:21:12,825
You'll have to wait for me.

286
00:21:51,865 --> 00:21:53,145
Why are you back?

287
00:21:53,745 --> 00:21:55,825
I came back to report something for work,
then I'm leaving.

288
00:22:02,265 --> 00:22:03,425
I missed you.

289
00:22:28,105 --> 00:22:28,945
Everyone,

290
00:22:29,665 --> 00:22:33,305
to more efficiently advance
the New Media campaign

291
00:22:33,385 --> 00:22:34,705
for Xizi Cultural Tourism Group,

292
00:22:35,305 --> 00:22:37,265
the company has decided
to form a dedicated project team

293
00:22:38,105 --> 00:22:40,705
to be stationed on-site
for in-depth operations.

294
00:22:41,225 --> 00:22:42,345
The team members are as follows.

295
00:22:42,425 --> 00:22:43,465
Kitty.

296
00:22:44,425 --> 00:22:46,185
Claire. Leo.

297
00:22:46,265 --> 00:22:47,825
Kangkang. Sunny.

298
00:22:47,905 --> 00:22:49,505
Kami. William.

299
00:22:49,585 --> 00:22:51,305
Lucy. Flora.

300
00:22:55,065 --> 00:22:56,505
Dony.

301
00:22:56,585 --> 00:22:59,865
I've always been responsible
for the Beijing New Media team.

302
00:22:59,945 --> 00:23:01,225
I won't be going this time.

303
00:23:01,305 --> 00:23:02,945
I'll stay in Beijing
and support all of you.

304
00:23:03,745 --> 00:23:05,625
Anyone can opt out, except you.

305
00:23:06,905 --> 00:23:09,385
You'll be leading
this dedicated project team.

306
00:23:11,265 --> 00:23:12,625
Let's wrap up the meeting here.

307
00:23:21,065 --> 00:23:22,105
Flora.

308
00:23:22,185 --> 00:23:23,345
Come have a seat.

309
00:23:33,665 --> 00:23:35,865
I've read your report on this project.

310
00:23:35,945 --> 00:23:37,225
You did an excellent job.

311
00:23:37,745 --> 00:23:39,145
You identified the key issues
very accurately.

312
00:23:40,065 --> 00:23:43,025
And the three core client concerns
you raised

313
00:23:43,625 --> 00:23:46,305
are exactly what we need
to address first at the workshop.

314
00:23:47,225 --> 00:23:48,225
Well done.

315
00:23:48,305 --> 00:23:49,625
Thank you, Dony.

316
00:23:54,265 --> 00:23:57,065
Do you trust Luke?

317
00:24:01,705 --> 00:24:05,225
Luke is very capable,
and he's strict with all of us.

318
00:24:05,305 --> 00:24:07,705
We've learned a lot from him.

319
00:24:07,785 --> 00:24:09,345
We all respect him.

320
00:24:11,265 --> 00:24:13,425
Flora, you need to understand this.

321
00:24:14,305 --> 00:24:17,225
Anyone in that position,
with the resources it comes with,

322
00:24:17,825 --> 00:24:19,305
would appear highly capable.

323
00:24:20,025 --> 00:24:22,305
Anyone in that position
would have that halo.

324
00:24:22,905 --> 00:24:24,745
Don't be blinded by it.

325
00:24:27,145 --> 00:24:28,105
I looked into your background.

326
00:24:28,185 --> 00:24:29,545
You earned your place
in the New Media Division

327
00:24:29,625 --> 00:24:30,705
through open competition.

328
00:24:31,465 --> 00:24:34,025
This project is another opportunity.

329
00:24:34,625 --> 00:24:36,745
You can learn just as much
by working with me,

330
00:24:36,825 --> 00:24:39,305
and you'll be promoted much faster.

331
00:24:49,505 --> 00:24:52,305
Dony is clearly trying to poach people
and expand his team.

332
00:24:52,385 --> 00:24:54,425
Are you sure you want to take leave
at a time like this?

333
00:24:55,105 --> 00:24:57,225
So you're saying
I should fight for it too?

334
00:24:57,825 --> 00:24:59,745
Have two opposing pawns
fight tooth and nail,

335
00:25:00,585 --> 00:25:04,225
so the board can sit back
and enjoy the show?

336
00:25:06,425 --> 00:25:08,865
I guess you're retreating to advance.

337
00:25:09,985 --> 00:25:13,305
But you've retreated too far,
letting your opponent seize the advantage.

338
00:25:13,385 --> 00:25:16,665
It won't be easy
to turn things around after that.

339
00:25:20,665 --> 00:25:21,825
Senior,

340
00:25:22,785 --> 00:25:24,665
thank you for putting up with me
all these years.

341
00:25:25,225 --> 00:25:27,585
And no matter what,
you've always been on my side.

342
00:25:28,505 --> 00:25:31,265
But I'd also ask you
to keep an eye on the new guy.

343
00:25:31,945 --> 00:25:33,865
If he really goes too far,

344
00:25:33,945 --> 00:25:36,825
we'll be the ones
left to clean up the mess.

345
00:25:38,225 --> 00:25:39,305
Exactly.

346
00:25:39,385 --> 00:25:40,865
That's what I'm worried about.

347
00:25:41,505 --> 00:25:43,905
Today the board can bypass us
and bring in Dony.

348
00:25:43,985 --> 00:25:47,265
Tomorrow they could easily
send us an HRBP.

349
00:25:48,305 --> 00:25:50,145
Hurry up and process my annual leave.

350
00:25:50,665 --> 00:25:51,745
I'm taking some time off to clear my head.

351
00:25:52,345 --> 00:25:54,145
If I'm in a good mood,

352
00:25:54,225 --> 00:25:55,905
I might even help you prepare
for what's coming.

353
00:25:57,705 --> 00:25:58,825
Thanks, Junior.

354
00:25:58,905 --> 00:26:00,025
You're welcome.

355
00:26:00,825 --> 00:26:02,425
Thank you, my dear Senior.

356
00:26:14,345 --> 00:26:16,185
Dony's a really nice guy.

357
00:26:16,265 --> 00:26:17,985
He doesn't put on airs at all.

358
00:26:18,065 --> 00:26:19,505
Yesterday, he even asked me

359
00:26:19,585 --> 00:26:22,145
if work was going smoothly
and whether I lived far away.

360
00:26:22,945 --> 00:26:24,465
He really is easy to get along with.

361
00:26:24,545 --> 00:26:25,585
He asked me yesterday too.

362
00:26:25,665 --> 00:26:27,665
He wanted to know what I like to do

363
00:26:27,745 --> 00:26:29,625
and what I usually do on weekends.

364
00:26:29,705 --> 00:26:31,105
He even asked if I had a boyfriend.

365
00:26:31,185 --> 00:26:34,385
He said there are a lot of outstanding
young men at headquarters

366
00:26:34,465 --> 00:26:35,785
and that I should get
to know some of them.

367
00:26:38,185 --> 00:26:39,225
Tao.

368
00:26:44,825 --> 00:26:48,345
Dony's way of winning people over
is really straightforward.

369
00:26:49,105 --> 00:26:50,985
I heard the board
sent him to replace Luke.

370
00:26:53,065 --> 00:26:54,945
The board isn't happy with Luke.

371
00:26:55,025 --> 00:26:55,865
They think he's too hard to manage.

372
00:27:18,345 --> 00:27:20,625
Where did this young golden boy come from?

373
00:27:23,465 --> 00:27:24,945
Excuse me. Who's Lumi?

374
00:27:27,545 --> 00:27:28,385
I am.

375
00:27:30,905 --> 00:27:31,745
And you are?

376
00:27:50,385 --> 00:27:51,545
What's going on?

377
00:27:53,265 --> 00:27:55,825
I don't know
where HR found this old academic.

378
00:27:56,425 --> 00:27:58,985
What kind of so-called
marketing expert is he?

379
00:27:59,065 --> 00:28:01,025
Why do I have to report everything to him?

380
00:28:01,105 --> 00:28:02,345
Even Luan Nian couldn't control me.

381
00:28:02,425 --> 00:28:05,825
Now he's setting all these rules
for me to follow.

382
00:28:05,905 --> 00:28:07,105
Why should I?

383
00:28:08,305 --> 00:28:09,465
What's going on?

384
00:28:11,745 --> 00:28:13,225
Luke just went on leave,

385
00:28:13,305 --> 00:28:15,705
and the company brings in
this marketing expert.

386
00:28:18,105 --> 00:28:19,185
This Will…

387
00:28:19,265 --> 00:28:22,545
Could Dony have sent him
to make things difficult for me?

388
00:28:23,665 --> 00:28:24,505
No, wait.

389
00:28:24,585 --> 00:28:27,385
Dony can even interfere
with HR's responsibilities now?

390
00:28:28,785 --> 00:28:30,065
On this business trip,

391
00:28:30,145 --> 00:28:32,305
you have to keep a close eye
on things for Luan Nian.

392
00:28:34,505 --> 00:28:35,425
Don't worry.

393
00:28:39,025 --> 00:28:39,865
No.

394
00:28:40,385 --> 00:28:41,265
I can't just sit back and do nothing.

395
00:28:41,945 --> 00:28:44,625
I have to find out
where this old academic came from.

396
00:28:58,985 --> 00:29:01,545
HANGZHOU

397
00:29:01,625 --> 00:29:02,545
-Dony.
-You're here.

398
00:29:03,985 --> 00:29:05,265
Have a seat.

399
00:29:08,105 --> 00:29:09,785
Flora. Don't sit by the door.

400
00:29:09,865 --> 00:29:11,185
Sit over here.

401
00:29:22,345 --> 00:29:23,505
Dony.

402
00:29:23,585 --> 00:29:25,905
This fish
is this restaurant's signature dish.

403
00:29:25,985 --> 00:29:27,225
Please, try some.

404
00:29:31,025 --> 00:29:32,065
You first.

405
00:29:32,585 --> 00:29:33,585
Thank you.

406
00:29:35,465 --> 00:29:39,465
I think the key visual
for this project is extremely creative.

407
00:29:39,545 --> 00:29:41,065
Kangkang did a great job.

408
00:29:41,825 --> 00:29:43,185
Thank you, Dony. Just doing my job.

409
00:29:44,105 --> 00:29:45,065
No need to be so polite.

410
00:29:45,785 --> 00:29:48,505
Now that our dedicated project team
has been formed, we're one family.

411
00:29:48,585 --> 00:29:50,025
We're one team.

412
00:29:50,105 --> 00:29:50,985
Just call me Dony.

413
00:29:51,065 --> 00:29:52,825
Treat this like you're at home.

414
00:29:53,505 --> 00:29:56,065
Relax, everyone. Don't hold back.

415
00:29:56,145 --> 00:29:57,185
Come on. Cheers.

416
00:29:58,505 --> 00:30:01,065
I… I can't drink.
I'll toast with water instead.

417
00:30:02,185 --> 00:30:04,185
I don't drink much either.
I'll use tea instead.

418
00:30:05,265 --> 00:30:07,425
It's just wine. One glass won't hurt.

419
00:30:07,505 --> 00:30:09,105
It's even good for your skin.

420
00:30:09,185 --> 00:30:10,305
Just one glass.

421
00:30:10,905 --> 00:30:11,905
Here.

422
00:30:25,705 --> 00:30:29,865
This toast is to wish
our dedicated project team

423
00:30:29,945 --> 00:30:32,945
great success here in Hangzhou.

424
00:30:33,025 --> 00:30:33,905
Cheers.

425
00:30:36,025 --> 00:30:37,065
To a great success.

426
00:30:38,785 --> 00:30:40,305
Kangkang, it's okay.

427
00:30:40,385 --> 00:30:41,585
If you don't want to drink, don't.

428
00:30:42,185 --> 00:30:43,505
At Lime, we have a tradition.

429
00:30:43,585 --> 00:30:44,825
We drink, but we never pressure anyone to.

430
00:30:44,905 --> 00:30:47,105
Especially not our female employees.

431
00:30:49,945 --> 00:30:52,865
Dony, you were just excited, right?

432
00:30:52,945 --> 00:30:54,625
He was only asking us to take a sip.

433
00:30:57,185 --> 00:30:58,225
Flora's right.

434
00:31:00,865 --> 00:31:02,385
Just a sip is enough. Don't drink anymore.

435
00:31:06,625 --> 00:31:08,785
Flora. Do you have a boyfriend?

436
00:31:12,145 --> 00:31:15,225
That's a private matter,
so I'd rather not say.

437
00:31:15,985 --> 00:31:17,425
Why keep it a secret?

438
00:31:17,985 --> 00:31:20,585
I don't mind saying it. I'm single.

439
00:31:24,945 --> 00:31:25,985
Dony,

440
00:31:27,625 --> 00:31:28,945
this toast is for you.

441
00:31:29,585 --> 00:31:32,025
Thank you for bringing us here to learn.

442
00:31:32,865 --> 00:31:34,705
Take your time. I'll finish mine.

443
00:31:45,625 --> 00:31:46,825
Look at Kitty.

444
00:31:47,825 --> 00:31:51,225
That's what I call bringing energy to work
and passion to life.

445
00:31:52,305 --> 00:31:53,585
Everyone should learn from her.

446
00:31:54,265 --> 00:31:55,265
Come on.

447
00:32:02,585 --> 00:32:03,585
I need to take this. Excuse me.

448
00:32:13,705 --> 00:32:15,105
A stroke?

449
00:32:15,785 --> 00:32:17,225
When did it happen?

450
00:32:17,825 --> 00:32:18,865
Is it serious?

451
00:32:19,705 --> 00:32:20,745
They caught it in time.

452
00:32:20,825 --> 00:32:21,825
He's not in any danger.

453
00:32:24,905 --> 00:32:26,025
I'm calling because

454
00:32:26,105 --> 00:32:28,145
I've got an urgent job
that has to be submitted today.

455
00:32:28,225 --> 00:32:29,665
You worked on this project before,

456
00:32:30,345 --> 00:32:32,465
so I was hoping you could help me.

457
00:32:33,545 --> 00:32:34,425
Don't worry.

458
00:32:34,505 --> 00:32:35,665
I'll take care of all the work for you.

459
00:32:36,265 --> 00:32:38,505
Can you handle everything
at the hospital by yourself?

460
00:32:38,585 --> 00:32:39,585
I think so.

461
00:32:39,665 --> 00:32:41,745
My mom and I are taking shifts,
and we'll hire a caregiver.

462
00:32:42,345 --> 00:32:44,665
I'll be at the hospital
the next couple of days.

463
00:32:44,745 --> 00:32:48,465
I'm just worried
that jerk Will won't approve my leave.

464
00:32:49,425 --> 00:32:52,185
He can't be that unreasonable.

465
00:32:52,265 --> 00:32:53,585
You never know.

466
00:32:54,385 --> 00:32:56,145
He just chewed me out
at yesterday's meeting.

467
00:32:56,225 --> 00:32:59,585
For clocking in and out on time
and being irresponsible.

468
00:32:59,665 --> 00:33:00,745
What an old fossil.

469
00:33:01,345 --> 00:33:03,305
What's wrong with clocking
in and out on time? What's wrong?

470
00:33:03,905 --> 00:33:05,745
Exactly. He doesn't know
how good our Lumi is

471
00:33:05,825 --> 00:33:07,865
at managing her time.

472
00:33:07,945 --> 00:33:11,705
Now I'm completely convinced
he's Dony's plant.

473
00:33:11,785 --> 00:33:13,985
They're trying to drive away
that stubborn mule's right-hand men,

474
00:33:14,065 --> 00:33:15,465
and once they do, they've won.

475
00:33:18,065 --> 00:33:19,545
How are things on Dony's side?

476
00:33:20,065 --> 00:33:20,905
Busy?

477
00:33:23,145 --> 00:33:24,545
Not at all. Everything's going well.

478
00:33:25,625 --> 00:33:27,625
If you need anything, just let me know.

479
00:33:27,705 --> 00:33:29,265
I'll handle it for you remotely.

480
00:33:30,465 --> 00:33:32,305
It won't affect work at all. Don't worry.

481
00:33:33,985 --> 00:33:34,825
Okay.

482
00:33:34,905 --> 00:33:35,985
Then I'll take you up on that.

483
00:33:36,065 --> 00:33:37,665
I'll go ask for leave.

484
00:33:38,385 --> 00:33:43,185
I'm sure that old fossil
is only going to ask one thing.

485
00:33:44,065 --> 00:33:44,905
The reason?

486
00:33:45,945 --> 00:33:47,465
My father was hospitalized after a stroke.

487
00:33:50,945 --> 00:33:52,185
Submit your leave request
through the proper process.

488
00:33:52,265 --> 00:33:53,545
Make sure your work
is properly handed over.

489
00:33:57,425 --> 00:33:58,625
That's it?

490
00:34:01,065 --> 00:34:02,185
What else?

491
00:34:06,985 --> 00:34:08,105
Thanks.

492
00:34:09,705 --> 00:34:10,824
Close the door.

493
00:35:31,945 --> 00:35:33,945
‎I feel there’s still a bit of an issue.

494
00:35:34,025 --> 00:35:36,065
Check this line.

495
00:35:36,145 --> 00:35:37,465
I think there's a problem.

496
00:35:37,545 --> 00:35:38,745
I'll check it.

497
00:35:39,425 --> 00:35:40,465
Just leave it here.

498
00:35:40,545 --> 00:35:41,465
Flora.

499
00:35:46,185 --> 00:35:47,225
Kitty.

500
00:35:53,585 --> 00:35:54,425
Flora.

501
00:35:55,385 --> 00:35:58,345
Why does this budget
have to be approved by Luke?

502
00:35:59,745 --> 00:36:02,265
Lime's budget management
has three core components.

503
00:36:02,345 --> 00:36:04,785
They include the approval process
and time limits.

504
00:36:04,865 --> 00:36:06,625
They're all clearly defined.

505
00:36:06,705 --> 00:36:08,905
Dony, you should know that, shouldn't you?

506
00:36:10,745 --> 00:36:11,705
All right.

507
00:36:12,225 --> 00:36:13,945
I'll follow the budget approval process.

508
00:36:14,025 --> 00:36:15,105
I'll get going.

509
00:36:28,905 --> 00:36:31,785
None of the top MCN resources
from our Beijing office can be used.

510
00:36:31,865 --> 00:36:33,945
Everything has to go through
the Hangzhou headquarters now.

511
00:36:34,025 --> 00:36:35,785
Isn't that basically
starting from scratch?

512
00:36:36,545 --> 00:36:39,825
The client just asked me
why this New Media campaign

513
00:36:39,905 --> 00:36:41,825
was suddenly moved
from Beijing to Hangzhou.

514
00:36:42,785 --> 00:36:44,425
They think the Beijing team
is more experienced

515
00:36:44,505 --> 00:36:45,625
and has better resources.

516
00:36:45,705 --> 00:36:46,585
They're concerned about the results.

517
00:36:47,545 --> 00:36:48,985
I didn't even know how to explain it.

518
00:36:50,585 --> 00:36:54,105
Just tell them
Hangzhou is an emerging city

519
00:36:54,185 --> 00:36:57,105
with enormous potential
that's poised for rapid growth.

520
00:36:57,185 --> 00:36:58,505
Potential?

521
00:36:58,585 --> 00:36:59,825
Based on the data,

522
00:36:59,905 --> 00:37:02,265
how does Hangzhou's new media ecosystem
or top-tier resources

523
00:37:02,345 --> 00:37:03,945
compare to Beijing's?

524
00:37:04,785 --> 00:37:06,065
The resources aren't there.

525
00:37:06,145 --> 00:37:07,305
The client's concerned.

526
00:37:07,385 --> 00:37:08,785
And the team's working themselves
to the bone.

527
00:37:10,585 --> 00:37:11,425
Where's Dony?

528
00:37:12,385 --> 00:37:14,265
I heard he's out
doing market research again.

529
00:37:14,945 --> 00:37:16,025
I saw Dony

530
00:37:16,105 --> 00:37:18,065
downstairs this morning
carrying a pot of orchids.

531
00:37:18,145 --> 00:37:19,425
They were beautiful.

532
00:37:19,505 --> 00:37:21,385
You could tell they were expensive.

533
00:37:21,465 --> 00:37:23,425
Yeah. Yesterday it was an art gallery.

534
00:37:23,505 --> 00:37:25,065
The day before, a tea house.

535
00:37:25,145 --> 00:37:26,225
So what came of all that research?

536
00:37:26,305 --> 00:37:27,945
How are we supposed
to explain it to the client?

537
00:37:28,025 --> 00:37:31,185
Tell them our boss went off
to drink tea and admire flowers?

538
00:37:31,265 --> 00:37:32,665
Let's just focus on our own work for now.

539
00:37:32,745 --> 00:37:34,065
When Dony gets back,

540
00:37:34,145 --> 00:37:36,345
ask him to give us clearer instructions
as soon as possible.

541
00:37:47,305 --> 00:37:49,505
BUDGET REQUEST APPROVED

542
00:37:49,585 --> 00:37:52,945
Why does this budget
have to be approved by Luke?

543
00:37:58,705 --> 00:37:59,865
Hello?

544
00:37:59,945 --> 00:38:02,265
-Did I interrupt you?
-No.

545
00:38:03,145 --> 00:38:04,585
I was walking Luke.

546
00:38:04,665 --> 00:38:05,785
What's up?

547
00:38:07,705 --> 00:38:11,305
Did you receive
the two budget requests from Dony?

548
00:38:11,385 --> 00:38:12,265
No.

549
00:38:13,305 --> 00:38:15,465
Is Dony in a rush
and asked you to follow up with me?

550
00:38:15,545 --> 00:38:16,665
No.

551
00:38:16,745 --> 00:38:18,065
According to the process,

552
00:38:18,145 --> 00:38:20,025
those two budget requests need your
signature before they can take effect.

553
00:38:20,105 --> 00:38:21,505
But somehow they skipped you.

554
00:38:22,345 --> 00:38:24,505
I've already received
the payment notification.

555
00:38:26,265 --> 00:38:28,265
I don't think the system
would miss something like that.

556
00:38:30,145 --> 00:38:31,145
Got it.

557
00:38:32,065 --> 00:38:33,705
Has he given you
a hard time anywhere else?

558
00:38:34,425 --> 00:38:35,345
No.

559
00:38:35,425 --> 00:38:37,225
He's hardly ever in the office.

560
00:38:39,225 --> 00:38:41,985
By the way, give me Sun Yu's number.

561
00:38:42,065 --> 00:38:44,025
A friend of mine in investment banking
wants to meet her.

562
00:38:45,025 --> 00:38:46,265
Maybe they'll invest in her.

563
00:38:50,785 --> 00:38:51,705
Thank you.

564
00:38:52,545 --> 00:38:53,665
I mean it.

565
00:38:55,985 --> 00:38:57,225
All right, then.

566
00:39:00,865 --> 00:39:02,025
Let's go. Luke.

567
00:39:20,305 --> 00:39:21,385
Coming.

568
00:39:27,625 --> 00:39:29,585
-Kitty.
-Flora.

569
00:39:30,385 --> 00:39:32,065
Sorry to bother you so late.

570
00:39:32,625 --> 00:39:33,705
Could you do me a favor?

571
00:39:34,785 --> 00:39:35,745
Sure.

572
00:39:40,345 --> 00:39:43,545
Could you report to Dony for me?

573
00:39:45,225 --> 00:39:46,465
Me?

574
00:39:47,065 --> 00:39:48,025
Yes.

575
00:39:48,785 --> 00:39:51,305
I… I still have some backend data
to finish processing.

576
00:39:51,385 --> 00:39:52,585
I'm a little pressed for time.

577
00:39:53,265 --> 00:39:55,265
But I've already finished the proposal.

578
00:39:57,385 --> 00:39:58,425
No problem. I'll go.

579
00:40:00,425 --> 00:40:01,625
Great. Thanks.

580
00:40:02,305 --> 00:40:03,185
No problem.

581
00:40:05,625 --> 00:40:06,665
Flora.

582
00:40:08,865 --> 00:40:11,225
If anything comes up later,
call me anytime.

583
00:40:11,305 --> 00:40:14,025
I'll be around. I can come over.

584
00:40:15,385 --> 00:40:17,265
Don't you need
to finish processing the data?

585
00:40:18,665 --> 00:40:23,625
Yeah. But Dony
can be pretty particular about work.

586
00:40:23,705 --> 00:40:25,785
When you report to him,

587
00:40:25,865 --> 00:40:27,505
pay attention to how you approach it.

588
00:40:30,705 --> 00:40:31,545
Don't worry.

589
00:40:34,745 --> 00:40:35,785
Okay.

590
00:40:55,625 --> 00:40:56,625
Why haven't you left yet?

591
00:40:59,945 --> 00:41:01,225
Let's go together.

592
00:41:09,105 --> 00:41:10,145
Flora.

593
00:41:12,665 --> 00:41:13,705
Kitty.

594
00:41:17,065 --> 00:41:17,945
Kitty.

595
00:41:30,105 --> 00:41:31,665
Are you afraid of Dony?

596
00:41:36,385 --> 00:41:37,585
The background check results are in.

597
00:41:38,625 --> 00:41:40,745
During his time at his previous company,

598
00:41:40,825 --> 00:41:42,705
Dony came under strong suspicion
of embezzlement.

599
00:41:44,345 --> 00:41:46,185
And it involved
a substantial amount of money.

600
00:41:49,665 --> 00:41:50,505
Specifically?

601
00:41:51,225 --> 00:41:54,225
He skimmed money through price differences
in supplier contracts.

602
00:41:54,305 --> 00:41:55,985
It wasn't a particularly
sophisticated scheme,

603
00:41:56,065 --> 00:41:58,905
but the investigation was quietly dropped.

604
00:41:59,505 --> 00:42:01,945
He left the company on the grounds
of personal career development.

605
00:42:02,665 --> 00:42:04,505
That does fit his usual style.

606
00:42:04,585 --> 00:42:06,705
I don't get it.

607
00:42:06,785 --> 00:42:09,225
How could someone with such
a serious black mark on his record

608
00:42:09,825 --> 00:42:13,745
be parachuted in by the board
to keep you in check?

609
00:42:15,745 --> 00:42:17,425
Who was it on the board
that brought Dony in?

610
00:42:18,705 --> 00:42:20,225
Mr. He. He Qiming.

611
00:42:22,105 --> 00:42:25,145
Last year, He Qiming strongly backed
that Southeast Asia project.

612
00:42:25,225 --> 00:42:27,105
I joined forces with several shareholders
to vote it down.

613
00:42:27,705 --> 00:42:29,185
I guess he felt humiliated.

614
00:42:29,745 --> 00:42:31,545
Divide and balance power. Create chaos.

615
00:42:32,665 --> 00:42:34,665
He just wants to see me fail.

616
00:42:34,745 --> 00:42:35,785
It's obvious.

617
00:42:36,705 --> 00:42:40,225
So, Dony works for him?

618
00:42:41,065 --> 00:42:42,305
More like a puppet.

619
00:42:42,945 --> 00:42:46,625
A puppet who's willing
to go head-to-head with me.

620
00:43:08,865 --> 00:43:11,585
Dony, we're here
to give you a work update.

621
00:43:15,785 --> 00:43:17,785
Could he be laundering money for Mr. He?

622
00:43:18,305 --> 00:43:19,705
Send Lumi to Hangzhou.

623
00:43:20,345 --> 00:43:22,345
Follow the trail back to the source.

624
00:43:23,105 --> 00:43:24,065
No.

625
00:43:24,145 --> 00:43:26,385
Lumi is known to be your right hand.

626
00:43:26,465 --> 00:43:28,545
If you do that, won't you tip them off?

627
00:43:29,625 --> 00:43:30,705
That's exactly the point.

628
00:43:31,585 --> 00:43:35,745
I want Lumi to openly investigate
the cash flow, ownership structure,

629
00:43:35,825 --> 00:43:38,265
and beneficial owners
behind those companies.

630
00:43:38,345 --> 00:43:39,785
Peel back the layers,

631
00:43:39,865 --> 00:43:41,385
and eventually we'll expose
the person behind it all.

632
00:43:44,065 --> 00:43:45,185
You're good at this.

633
00:44:19,705 --> 00:44:20,905
You're still up?

634
00:44:23,705 --> 00:44:27,305
Sun Yu's project
isn't performing very well.

635
00:44:27,385 --> 00:44:28,985
I'm helping her revise her business plan.

636
00:44:37,465 --> 00:44:38,945
Sun Yu's making a dating app?

637
00:44:40,385 --> 00:44:42,825
Take a look at this proposal for me.

638
00:44:42,905 --> 00:44:44,625
You're the expert
when it comes to investments.

639
00:44:56,745 --> 00:44:58,105
The business plan isn't strong enough.

640
00:44:58,185 --> 00:44:59,145
The data isn't convincing enough.

641
00:44:59,905 --> 00:45:01,145
And the key selling points
don't stand out.

642
00:45:03,105 --> 00:45:04,385
Then,

643
00:45:05,825 --> 00:45:08,745
how can a proposal attract investors?

644
00:45:09,345 --> 00:45:12,305
Shang Zhitao, I'm on leave,
and you're still making me work.

645
00:45:23,305 --> 00:45:24,985
It's not like
you've got anything else to do.

646
00:45:25,785 --> 00:45:27,345
Help me polish the business plan.

647
00:45:34,785 --> 00:45:36,065
Now you're pushing your luck.

